# System Overview

The proposed system consists of five major components:

## 1. Ground Detection Nodes

Solar-powered camera stations continuously monitor their local area.

Each node:

- Detects motion
- Captures images
- Runs AI classification
- Reports detected species
- Operates autonomously

### Typical Node Components

- Raspberry Pi Zero 2W
- Camera Module
- Solar Panel
- Battery System
- LoRa Radio
- Weatherproof Enclosure

---

## 2. Low-Power Communications Network

Detection nodes communicate using LoRa technology.

Benefits include:

- Long range operation
- Low power consumption
- Simple infrastructure requirements
- Excellent rural coverage

Typical ranges:

| Environment | Expected Range |
|------------|------------|
| Dense bush | 2-5 km |
| Open farmland | 5-10 km |
| Line of sight | 10+ km |

---

## 3. Central Command Server

A central Raspberry Pi-based server acts as the decision-making component.

Functions include:

- Event collection
- Image processing
- Confidence scoring
- Alert management
- Drone dispatching
- Data storage

Example workflow:

```text
Detection Received
↓
Species Confirmed
↓
Confidence Calculated
↓
Launch Decision
```

---

## 4. Autonomous Drone Platform

Rather than continuously patrolling, drones are launched only when required.

Responsibilities include:

- Investigation of detections
- Additional imagery collection
- Species verification
- Behaviour observation
- Follow-up monitoring

This significantly reduces energy consumption compared with constant aerial patrols.

---

## 5. Solar-Powered Charging Stations

Charging stations provide:

- Drone landing platforms
- Battery charging
- Communications relay
- Mission staging

These stations enable the drone to operate across large areas without always returning to a central base.

---

# Core Operating Concept

The operating model centres around event-driven drone deployment.

### Conventional Approach

```text
Drone Patrols Continuously
↓
High Battery Usage
↓
Limited Observation Time
```

### Proposed Approach

```text
Ground Sensors Monitor Environment
↓
Predator Detected
↓
Command Server Evaluates Event
↓
Drone Dispatched
↓
Drone Investigates
↓
Drone Lands on Perch Station
↓
Long-Term Observation
```

This architecture shifts the primary monitoring workload to low-cost ground sensors while reserving drone resources for targeted investigations.

