# Conclusion

This project presents a practical development pathway from an existing Raspberry Pi predator camera system to a fully autonomous monitoring network. By progressing through carefully defined phases, technical risks can be addressed incrementally while building valuable capability at each stage.

The immediate focus is deployment of AI-based wildlife classification on the existing Raspberry Pi platform. Success at this stage establishes the foundation upon which the larger sensor network and autonomous drone infrastructure can be built.

**Recommended Next Step:** Complete Phase 1 by integrating YOLO-based wildlife classification into the current Raspberry Pi predator detection system and begin collecting a custom New Zealand predator image dataset.